@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# Korean (한국어) interface
+
+> **Added:** 2026-10-13 on top of v0.9.2 (470ea7a3) · **Code:** `ko` · **Status:** complete against the current catalogs, not yet reviewed by a native speaker
+
+EffectCraft's interface in Korean, with the terminology of the Korean edition of After Effects.
+How languages are wired in general: [localization-parity.md](localization-parity.md).
+
+## Provenance
+
+- **Written from scratch.** There was no upstream Korean translation (#616 only made the
+  interface probe for a Hangul font so Korean *names* are not drawn as boxes). No Adobe text was
+  copied; the wording follows the Korean After Effects terms a Korean user already knows (table
+  below), applied to EffectCraft's own English source strings.
+- **AI-assisted** (Claude Opus 5.5), checked mechanically by the tests below. It has not yet been
+  proofread by a native speaker: corrections are welcome as pull requests against the two
+  `KOREAN` tables.
+- **Where the rows live:**
+  - menus: `KOREAN` in `crates/ui-egui/src/i18n.rs`, keyed by `(command, English label)`;
+  - panels, dialogs, buttons, tooltips: `KOREAN` in `crates/ui-egui/src/i18n/ui.rs`, keyed by the
+    English source string;
+  - computed labels (undo/redo, the platform's file manager, “…” workspace and 3D-view submenus,
+    macOS Services): the `"ko"` arms of `entry`, `label`, `submenu` and `native_menu.rs`.
+
+| Catalog | Reference rows | Korean rows | Copied verbatim (names only) | Newly translated |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Menus | 624 | 624 | 10 | 614 |
+| Panels | 506 | 506 | 4 | 502 |
+| **Total** | **1,130** | **1,130** | **14** | **1,116** |
+
+The reference is the most complete existing catalog (Simplified Chinese; Czech, Ukrainian and
+the others match it for menus and lag it for panels). The verbatim rows are names and
+technologies that stay as they are in every language: `EffectCraft`, `3D...`, `Lottie...`,
+`Lottie JSON...`, `ProEXR...`, `VR`, `RGB`, `SDTV NTSC`, `SDTV PAL`, `Display P3`, `Discord`,
+`URL:`, `▣ {}`.
+
+## Style
+
+- Menus, buttons and field names are short nouns or noun phrases, as in Korean Adobe apps
+  (`새 컴포지션...`, `레이어 설정...`, `모두 선택`).
+- Sentences (messages, hints, empty states) use the formal 합니다체 (`…없습니다`, `…하십시오`).
+- Never translated: placeholders (`{}` keeps its count and order: Korean word order was chosen
+  around them, e.g. `Step {} of {}: {}` → `{}/{}단계: {}`), units (`px`, `ms`, `fps`, `bpc`,
+  `kbps`, `%`, `°`), file formats and technologies (XML, JSON, Lottie, OpenEXR, PDF, Photoshop,
+  Premiere Pro, OpenGL, OCIO/ACES, Mercury, Opus, sRGB, Rec. 709…), product and community names.
+- `...` and `…` stay as in the English (the menus' dialog marker), and menu rows keep the
+  English number of parentheses.
+
+## Terminology
+
+| English | Korean |
+|---|---|
+| Composition / Comp | 컴포지션 |
+| Layer | 레이어 |
+| Timeline | 타임라인 |
+| Keyframe | 키프레임 |
+| Effects & Presets | 이펙트 및 사전 설정 |
+| Effect / Effect Controls | 이펙트 / 이펙트 컨트롤 |
+| Preset | 사전 설정 |
+| Pre-compose | 프리컴포즈 |
+| Mask / Mask Feather | 마스크 / 마스크 페더 |
+| Track Matte (Alpha / Luma Matte) | 트랙 매트 (알파 매트 / 루마 매트) |
+| Shape Layer | 셰이프 레이어 |
+| Text Animator | 텍스트 애니메이터 |
+| Graph Editor | 그래프 편집기 |
+| Easy Ease (In / Out) | 이지 이즈 (인 / 아웃) |
