+| Track Motion / Stabilize Motion | 모션 추적 / 모션 안정화 |
+| Time Remapping / Time Stretch | 시간 다시 매핑 / 시간 늘이기 |
+| Tutorial | 자습서 |
+
+## Language selection
+
+- Settings ▸ General ▸ Language ▸ **한국어** stores `general.language = "ko"`.
+- **Match System** selects Korean for every Korean locale: `ko`, `ko-KR`, `ko_KR.UTF-8`,
+  `KO_kr.UTF-8`, `ko-Kore-KR` (`supported()` in `i18n.rs`). A Korean Windows (ko-KR) therefore
+  opens in Korean with the default setting.
+
+## Fonts
+
+EffectCraft bundles no CJK font and Korean does **not** depend on craft-fonts (this app has no
+craft-fonts dependency at all; the release fonts are Inter, JetBrains Mono and Noto Serif). The
+interface draws Hangul with an **installed** face, found by `effectcraft_text::fonts::fallback_for`:
+
+- With Korean selected, `theme::install_script_fallbacks` probes Hangul (`한`) **first**, ahead of
+  the kana and Han probes, and sets the Korean CJK locale so Han characters prefer Korean faces too.
+  The Hangul face is added to every egui family (proportional, monospace, medium, semibold).
+- Families tried for Hangul, in order: Malgun Gothic, Gulim, Apple SD Gothic Neo, Noto Sans CJK KR,
+  Noto Sans KR, Source Han Sans KR, NanumGothic; then the Japanese and Chinese families (Noto Sans
+  CJK JP/SC also cover Hangul); then any installed face that covers it.
+- **Windows:** Malgun Gothic (`malgun.ttf`, family “Malgun Gothic”, Regular), part of every
+  Windows 10/11 install; Gulim if it is missing. The Regular face is used for all four UI families
+  (egui has no bold Hangul fallback). Han characters in a Korean UI are also drawn by Malgun Gothic.
+- **macOS:** Apple SD Gothic Neo. **Linux:** Noto Sans CJK KR / Noto Sans KR or another installed
+  Hangul font.
+- A catch-all face (Unifont) is never put first: if the Hangul face found also covers Arabic, it is
+  registered after the script-specific faces, as in the other languages.
+
+## Tests
+
+All in `effectcraft-ui-egui` (filtered `cargo test -p effectcraft-ui-egui --lib -- <filter>`):
+
+| Test | Checks |
+|---|---|
+| `i18n::tests::korean_menu_catalog_covers_every_reference_entry` | Korean menu keys = reference keys, no missing / extra, ≤ 40 untranslated copies |
+| `i18n::tests::every_translation_key_exists_in_the_actual_menu_tree` | every Korean key exists in the menu tree, every fixed tree entry is translated, same keys as every other language |
+| `i18n::tests::every_translated_entry_keeps_the_english_shape` | `...`, parentheses, no double spaces |
+| `i18n::tests::korean_translates_menus_without_changing_bindings_or_user_names` | command ids, params, shortcuts unchanged; key AE terms; user names verbatim; computed submenus |
+| `i18n::tests::korean_undo_redo_keeps_history_labels_verbatim` | 실행 취소 / 다시 실행 with history names verbatim |
+| `i18n::tests::korean_reveal_labels_follow_the_platform_file_manager` | Finder / 탐색기 / 파일 관리자 |
+| `i18n::tests::match_system_uses_the_system_language_where_there_is_a_catalog` | `ko`, `ko-KR`, `ko_KR.UTF-8`… → `ko` |
+| `i18n::tests::ukrainian_catalog_matches_the_settings_registry` | `("한국어", "ko")` in Settings ▸ Language, same order as the catalogs |
+| `i18n::ui::tests::korean_panel_catalog_covers_every_reference_row` | Korean panel rows = reference rows exactly |
+| `i18n::ui::tests::catalogs_are_unique_and_keep_the_english_shape` | placeholder counts equal the English |
+| `i18n::ui::tests::korean_panels_translate_and_keep_project_content_and_argument_order` | `tr` / `tr_args` order, names verbatim |
+| `i18n::ui::tests::every_row_is_used_by_a_converted_panel` | no stale Korean rows |
+| `theme::script_font_tests::korean_interface_draws_every_catalog_syllable` | every distinct Hangul syllable in both Korean catalogs draws a real glyph (not the replacement glyph) in all four UI families; skipped with a message when no Hangul font is installed |
+| `theme::tests::korean_interface_registers_the_hangul_face_first` | the Hangul face is registered first in a Korean UI, in every family; skipped with a message without one |
+| `native_menu::tests::korean_translates_macos_predefined_items` | 서비스 / EffectCraft 가리기 / 기타 가리기 / 모두 보기 (macOS only) |
+
+## Limits
+
+- Not proofread by a native speaker yet.
+- Like the other languages, only the catalogued strings are translated: effect names and their
+  parameters, engine messages (property names, errors, undo labels), unwrapped Home-screen and
+  panel literals and the Learn tutorials stay in English.
+- No bundled Hangul font: a machine with no Hangul font installed (some minimal Linux setups)
+  draws Korean as boxes; the web build has no system fonts at all, so Korean (like Japanese and
+  Chinese) is not usable there.
+- egui draws the UI with one Regular Hangul face; headings in semibold have no bold Hangul.
+- IME: the text tool (`panels/viewer_text.rs`) handles `egui::Event::Ime` — `Commit` inserts the
+  text through `text.insert`, `Preedit` is drawn as an underlined overlay at the caret (in the UI
+  face, not the layer's font) and the caret rectangle is sent as `IMEOutput` so the candidate
+  window follows it. egui-winit 0.36.2 drops IME-processed key presses on Windows (VK_PROCESSKEY),
+  so Backspace during Hangul composition does not also delete committed text. There is no
+  automated IME test and it has not been tried with the Windows Korean IME on a real machine.
